# Allowlist, not a blocklist. Everything is ignored, and only what is listed below is tracked.
#
# A blocklist leaks by omission: any file nobody thought to add a rule for ends up in the repository.
# This way a new local file, a tool output or a server directory is ignored until someone decides it
# belongs in the project. Add a line here when you want something published.

# Ignore every top-level entry, then re-add the ones that are source.
/*

# Repository files
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.editorconfig
!/LICENSE
!/README.md

# GitHub templates and workflows. CODEOWNERS stays out: the upstream one names upstream reviewers.
!/.github/
/.github/CODEOWNERS

# Gradle build
!/build.gradle.kts
!/settings.gradle.kts
!/gradle.properties
!/gradlew
!/gradlew.bat
!/gradle/
!/buildSrc/

# Source
!/common/
!/platforms/

# Inside the trees above, generated output and local state stay out. These are path-independent, so
# they apply at any depth.
build/
out/
run/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
.idea/
.vscode/
.fleet/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.class
*.log
*.hprof
hs_err_pid*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
